    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d849">

                <pb facs="0787" n="671" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg671"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 882.51/313B.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State
                        to the American Minister</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram—Extract.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-03-27">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">March 27, 1912</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Falkner has received notice that the Liberian Government will probably default on
                    interest of the 1871 loan unless he secures aid. He has been unable to do so.
                    Bankers can not understand why, with the receipts as reported, the Government
                    has not provided for this payment. They are skeptical as to whether correct
                    reports of receipts have been made. They want statement of receipts in the last
                    six months, and also want to know whether receipts reported for the last fiscal
                    year were actual cash receipts. Immediate action necessary, <pb facs="0788"
                        n="672" xml:id="pg672"/> as bankers have suspended further action pending
                    such report. Impress upon the Government that this matter is urgent and vital to
                    the continuation of the loan negotiations.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Wilson.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
